{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849987-defiance-of-red-surrender-2nd-edition-rules","id":849987,"title":"Defiance of Red Surrender 2nd Edition Rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-19T20:20:12-07:00","id":849987,"title":"Defiance of Red Surrender 2nd Edition Rules?","content":"What should the cost of the reverse of Red Surrender given losing dots is no longer a thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T21:06:53-07:00","id":850013,"title":"","content":"So, first, it took me some effort to find and figure out exactly what you're talking about, but I dug through the Gangrel Clanbook and found the sidebar I've never read before about defiance.<br /> <br /> Anyway, losing Willpower dots is totally a thing. I'm not sure what made you think it's not. It costs 1 XP to get a lost Willpower dot back, and there are still things that cost it. It is, admittedly, less common, but definitely still there. So, I would think that it would still cost a dot of Willpower, or, in other words, 1 XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T14:51:29-07:00","id":850260,"title":"","content":"A few weeks ago I tried drafting my own rules for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/838274-red-surrender-revisited\">Red Surrender, including my own take the Rumour of Defiance</a> sidebar. (My version lets you give up a Willpower Dot, similar to <i>Mandate from the Masses</i>; it's basically reserved to keep the Beast in check, and letting the Beast out of its containment also causes a Breaking Point.) If nothing else, maybe my version is a good starting point for something that works for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 03-21-2016, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T16:35:10-07:00","id":850308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849987-defiance-of-red-surrender-2nd-edition-rules?p=850013#post850013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, first, it took me some effort to find and figure out exactly what you're talking about, but I dug through the Gangrel Clanbook and found the sidebar I've never read before about defiance.<br /> <br /> Anyway, losing Willpower dots is totally a thing. I'm not sure what made you think it's not. It costs 1 XP to get a lost Willpower dot back, and there are still things that cost it. It is, admittedly, less common, but definitely still there. So, I would think that it would still cost a dot of Willpower, or, in other words, 1 XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the best of my knowledge give up a will power dot for anything has been cut out of second edition. The Devs didn't like the loss of states to do something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T17:57:20-07:00","id":850342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849987-defiance-of-red-surrender-2nd-edition-rules?p=850308#post850308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the best of my knowledge give up a will power dot for anything has been cut out of second edition. The Devs didn't like the loss of states to do something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why is there an xp cost for lost willpower dots? Aren't there even merits that cost willpower dots in blood and smoke?<br /> <br /> Is it just that you <i>want</i> some alternative cost? Because I would suggest it cost 1 XP, same as the willpower dot would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  Clarification 03-21-2016, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T22:00:32-07:00","id":850426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849987-defiance-of-red-surrender-2nd-edition-rules?p=850342#post850342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\\Aren't there even merits that cost willpower dots in blood and smoke?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The closest is Mandate from the Masses, which makes you temporarily lose access to a dot of willpower. But it comes back when (if) the effect ends.<br /> <br /> That said, Dave B. confirmed that there are things that cost permantent Willpower in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T22:50:01-07:00","id":850430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849987-defiance-of-red-surrender-2nd-edition-rules?p=850342#post850342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why is there an xp cost for lost willpower dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>Future proofing. In case something comes up later that costs a dot of willpower. You also might need it if you homebrew your own stuff that drains willpower dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-21-2016, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:38:04-07:00","id":850666,"title":"","content":"Actually calculating out the effect of this:<br /> -1 to 4 skills (-8 XP)<br /> -1 to Initiative (-1 XP, as +1 initiative is a merit)<br /> -1 to detect ambush/surprise (-1/2 XP, as the merit Danger Sense gives +2)<br /> -1 to derangement rolls (not a thing anymore)<br /> The defiance section makes it seem like the non-numerical bonuses don't apply, so, net of -9.5 XP in penalties<br /> <br /> +1 to 6 skills (12 XP)<br /> +1 to an attribute, but not to discipline rolls (3 XP, with an ad hoc -1 for not working with disciplines)<br /> +1 to detachment rolls (are you intending to keep this? The trade-off that balances this doesn't apply anymore).<br /> <br /> So, 15 XP - 9.5 XP = 5.5 XP. But, it's only one night per week, so, only a fraction of the time. Since you get to choose the night and circumstances, I might say it's not a full 1/7 as useful, maybe 1/4 or 1/5 as useful, which, yeah, leads to a rough equivalent in power to a 1 or 2 XP purchase (probably 2 if you keep the detachment bonus).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}